  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.0.0-preview.5\n\n\t\t=== Generative UI Level 2 - cards ===========================================\n\t\t- NEW - cards returned by a tool are forwarded to remote clients: a \"Cards\" hub event, and a {\"type\":\"cards\"} frame on the SSE stream. Additive - a client that ignores the new type still receives the whole answer as text.\n\t\t- Card frames are serialised camelCase with string enums, matching the rest of these endpoints; a JavaScript client reads \"kind\": \"navigate\" rather than a number whose meaning would shift if an enum member were inserted.\n\n\t\t=== Onboarding tour =========================================================\n\t\t- NEW - GET /mentor/tour returns the tour steps as JSON for headless and WASM clients, which have no access to the discovery data they are generated from. Enable it with EnableOnboardingTour on the server even though the client displays it.\n\t\t- Unauthenticated by design: the payload is the public screen names and capability descriptions the assistant already states in conversation, it is identical for every user, and generation is cached per process.\n\n\t\t=== Declarative agents ======================================================\n\t\t- Level-2 specialists supplied by an IMentorAgentSource - YAML definitions via the MentorAgent.Declarative package - are reachable over every transport with no protocol change.\n\n\t\t=== Documentation ===========================================================\n\t\t- The endpoint table now lists /mentor/approve, /mentor/cancel, /mentor/admin/metrics and /mentor/tour, not only the hub and the chat stream.",
